      "ISABEL: Irma Eckler. A Jewish woman.\nIRMA: An unexpected treat. You're early.",
      "MARION: Isabel Wilkerson's office.\nKATE: Hello. Hi. This is Kate. I'm Isabel's editor and I...\nMARION: I know your name. Hi, Kate. This is her cousin. Marion.\nKATE: Marion, hi. My condolences for your family's losses. I don't have the words. Unfathomable. Unthinkable.",
      "LIBRARIAN: What are you studying?\nELIZABETH: We work with Dr. Diedrich Westermann.",
      "NIGELLA: Everything Hitler is gone. They paved right over it all. And built new things.\nSABINE: You can literally walk right over Nazi places and not know it was ever there.",
